  "notes": "Cracked-belt power-pop written for maximum chorus impact. The drums are a terracing device rather than a groove: \"verses on a kick and finger snaps or a half-time snare; the chorus enters with a full four-square kick, layered claps and tom cascades. Fills are noise sweeps and reversed cymbals.\" So `kick.densityPerBar` runs 1—4 with `fourOnFloorInChorus` true, the snare stack is `snap` plus `clap`, and the fills are `riser`, `reverse` and `tom` lanes with the snare-roll ladder off — the reversed cymbal is a real lane, not a metaphor. The bass is explicitly not an 808: \"synth sub doubling the kick pattern; sub swell as the chorus trigger\", so the bassline is a kick mirror at 0.95 and no `bass808` block exists. Harmony is \"piano-led 4-bar loops with 7ths\" over \"minor keys with a IV—I plagal chorus cadence\", which is the top-weighted family. The entry's other harmonic claim — \"a raised third in the final chorus\" — is a Picardy third, a major tonic ending a minor song, not a raised seventh, so it is carried by the `major` weight in `session.scales` and no `harmonic_minor` is authored. The melody block encodes the entry's most useful claim — \"written topline-first for other artists as well as herself, so the shape is extremely standardised: narrow verse, rhythmically accelerating pre-chorus, then a chorus built on one held high note approached by leap\" — as `long_arc`, a wide `densityPerBar` spread for the acceleration, the highest melody register top in this batch, and an `octaveJumpProb` ceiling of 0.34 for that approach leap. \"Stacked octave doubles and wordless eh-vowel hooks\" is the `octave_echo` counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a medium-high rating because the research says the tempo band is \"partially inferred\": every drum probability and the humanize numbers are INFERRED. `bpm.mode` 118 is the entry's own stated power-ballad core. ⚠ The entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the cracked-top-note vocal claim is repeated here.",
